Data Briefing Cards — Ideation Decision Record
================================================
Date: 1 Apr 2026
Status: Exploratory prototype
Participants: Nhat (product), AI CDO agent

Context & Problem
-----------------
The KPI block approach hit an impasse:
- AI cannot encode business-specific formula decisions (e.g., what counts in "win rate")
- KPI specs need validation by someone who knows the data AND the business intent
- ~100 KPIs x 10 customers = unscalable hand-verification
- Each customer defines the same KPI differently ("spec drift")

Hypothesis: instead of making data fit a formula (KPI), start from the data, 
surface what it factually says, and let the user apply their own judgment.

Decision: Data Briefing Cards
-----------------------------
Replace KPI blocks with "Data Briefing Cards" — observation-based analysis 
that describes what the data shows, without prescribing formulas.

Card format (scannable, mobile-first, stock-ticker style):
- Theme: what the card is about
- Headline fact: one line, the most important thing
- Direction indicator: factual movement vs. last week (no good/bad judgment in v1)
- 2-3 supporting observations: notable patterns, anomalies, facts
- Source tag: which dataset(s) the card draws from

Three Lenses (User Chooses)
----------------------------
1. Data Domain — organized by data source (Pipeline, Shifts, Leads, Support)
2. Upcoming Decisions — organized by what the user is about to decide
3. Risks — organized by what could go wrong

Same underlying observations, different arrangement per lens.

User Interaction
----------------
- Default: user sees all cards
- User can pin favourites for "Monday morning scan"
- Cards are tappable for deeper detail

Weekly Exec Brief
-----------------
A composed narrative for Surge, pulling from all cards. Delivered weekly.
Covers: headline, platform activity, worth watching, data gaps.

LLM Role
--------
- Facts computed in code (counts, sums, comparisons)
- LLM writes observation narratives from computed facts
- Externally quality-checkable (another model or human can verify claims vs source data)
- Cross-source entity matching: AI fuzzy-match (e.g., "TWC" = "TerryWhite Chemmart")

Direction Indicator (v1)
------------------------
- Factual movement only (e.g., "down $200K vs last week")
- No good/bad judgment in v1
- User applies their own interpretation
- Future: layer in smart direction signals once we have user behaviour data

Prototype Scope
---------------
- Datasets: Deals + Shifts + cross-source
- Output: Markdown cards with real Locumate data
- All three lenses demonstrated
- See: decisions/Data-Briefing-Cards-Prototype-1Apr

Key Risks
---------
- LLM hallucination in observations — mitigate with code-computed facts
- "So what?" fatigue — value comes from cross-dataset connections and speed
- Scope creep — need curation layer driven by onboarding profile
- Fuzzy matching errors — "TWC" linking to wrong entity

Key Opportunities
-----------------
- Scales across customers (no per-customer formula definitions)
- Observations work regardless of data shape or column names
- Verifiability built in (every claim cites source + rows)
- Question Cards (future) could replace onboarding interview
